From b10c1d8fe14464407fc7f9aba2037f6760ee3142 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FAPO Integration <fapo-dev@example.local>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 04:05:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] scheduler: add FAPO control server and integrate it into
 the scheduler

Add lib/scheduler/fapo, a self-contained FAPO v1 control interface
(JSON Lines over TCP or Unix socket):

* fapo_telemetry.h: telemetry snapshots of the per-slice scheduler state
  (RB limits, priorities, pending DL/UL bytes, allocation rates,
  HARQ-derived loss) exchanged through a seqlock store (writer: slot
  thread, reader: control thread) and an MPMC command queue used to
  forward control actions to the slot loop.

* fapo_control_server: control server running on a dedicated non
  real-time thread. Implements the FAPO v1 protocol ops (hello, ping,
  get_telemetry, apply, reset) with per-slice validation and clamping of
  the requested RB limits to the cell capacity. The radio remains the
  source of truth: the effective policies are always echoed back in the
  telemetry.

* inter_slice_scheduler: collect real per-slice telemetry snapshots,
  apply new slice max RB limits (preserving the dedicated <= min <= max
  invariant) and restore the slice policies they were instantiated with
  on reset.

* ran_slice_instance: keep a copy of the baseline RRM policy
  configuration for the FAPO reset.

* ue_event_manager: cumulative DL HARQ ACK/NACK counters used to derive
  a real cell packet loss estimate.

* ue_scheduler_impl: publish telemetry snapshots and drain the pending
  control commands from the slot loop (non-blocking; commands are
  applied directly in the slot thread that owns the slice state).
  Commands targeting cells of other cell groups are pushed back into
  the shared queue.

* scheduler_impl: instantiate the FAPO context and control server when
  enabled and pass them to the cell group schedulers.
